          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જડવું (jaḍvũ) is listed by CDIAL as jaṛvũ, \"to join, meet with, set jewels\", under jaḍati, \"joins, sets\", a word that CDIAL takes from Dravidian, citing Bloch (CDIAL 5091). Of its senses, \"meet with\" is the nearest to \"to be found\"."
            }
          ]
